sentences.l:
So then having spoken she went away, and him she left there
incensed in heart for the well-girdled woman
whom by force, from him unwilling, they took away;

And they all day long with song and dance the god appeased,
singing a fair paean, the young men of the Achaeans,
celebrating the far-working one;

And they the mast set up and the white sails spread out,
and the wind filled the middle of the sail, and around, the wave
at the stem, surging, loudly resounded, as the ship went on;

But when they had come among the wide army of the Achaeans,
the black ship they for their part onto the dry land drew
high up on the sands, and under it long props stretched out;

But when from that time the twelfth dawn came to be,
then indeed to Olympus went the gods who are forever
all together, and Zeus led the way;
